# Tool run record integrity — test drive, not a construction.
#
# Proves SelfComparisonClaimShape catches the exact bug this session found in
# its own tooling: a run claiming a real, distinct baseline while its own
# recorded hashes are identical.
#
# TR_Lying: claims runConcludedDistinctBaseline true with matching hashes ->
#   violation, the exact real bug class.
# TR_Honest: claims true with genuinely different hashes -> silent.
# TR_HonestFalse: claims false (no distinct baseline available), matching
#   hashes -> silent; a tool that honestly reports "could not verify" is not
#   the failure this shape exists to catch.

@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/toolruntest#> .

ex:TS_Fixture a backlog:ToolScript ; backlog:scriptFileName "fixture_tool.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .

ex:TR_Lying a backlog:ToolRunRecord ; backlog:ranTool ex:TS_Fixture ;
    backlog:usedBaselineHash "abc123" ; backlog:comparedAgainstHash "abc123" ;
    backlog:runConcludedDistinctBaseline true .

ex:TR_Honest a backlog:ToolRunRecord ; backlog:ranTool ex:TS_Fixture ;
    backlog:usedBaselineHash "abc123" ; backlog:comparedAgainstHash "def456" ;
    backlog:runConcludedDistinctBaseline true .

ex:TR_HonestFalse a backlog:ToolRunRecord ; backlog:ranTool ex:TS_Fixture ;
    backlog:usedBaselineHash "abc123" ; backlog:comparedAgainstHash "abc123" ;
    backlog:runConcludedDistinctBaseline false .

# BaselineReferenceShape: BR_Bad missing its rationale -> fires. BR_Good complete -> silent.
ex:BR_Bad a backlog:BaselineReference ; backlog:baselineForTool ex:TS_Fixture ;
    backlog:hasBaselineLocation "https://example.org/fixture-only" .
ex:BR_Good a backlog:BaselineReference ; backlog:baselineForTool ex:TS_Fixture ;
    backlog:hasBaselineLocation "https://example.org/fixture-only" ;
    backlog:hasBaselineRationale "Fixture-only: a complete, real baseline reference." .

# v1.1.0 (2026-09-07) -- expected polarity declared on the fixture itself (TBox v1.82.0
# dropped the AdoptionProfile-only domain): Negative, because it exists to make the shape(s) named in its header FIRE; a run of it with no violation would mean that clause no longer fires (Polarity_Negative's own definition).
# Until now the gate inferred 'expected pass' from this filename and had no way to be right.
<http://example.org/toolruntest#> backlog:hasExpectedPolarity backlog:Polarity_Negative .
